Learning I love you and then saying to Robin exactly how he felt about dating and feeling lonely in New York and the pilot, is that there's this kind of old school wisdom in sitcoms, probably an hour dramas too, that goes the first six episodes, So in the first 10 episodes of your series, do the pilot six times.
在试播集中学会说“我爱你”，然后向罗宾准确表达他对约会和在纽约感到孤独的感受，情景喜剧里有一种老派的智慧，一小时剧情剧可能也是如此，那就是前六集，也就是剧集的前10集里，把试播集拍六次。

00:36:03.219 --> 00:36:12.219
Do the pilot six times so people really fucking get what the show is, and keep restating the premise, keep boom, boom, boom, find new ways to kind of say the same thing.
把试播集拍六次，好让观众他妈的真正明白这是一部什么样的剧，不断重申核心前提，不断地轰轰轰，用各种新方式去表达同一种东西。

00:36:12.219 --> 00:36:21.860
Obviously, you can't be that reductive and you need it to feel different, but I love that she's highlighting what this episode really was about and what the whole first season was about.
显然，你不能把它简化得那么绝对，你需要让它感觉有所不同，但我喜欢她点出了这一集的真正内核以及整个第一季的内核。

00:36:21.860 --> 00:36:22.860
